{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787949909435159001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unlit-asbestos-queenant","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ca7067db4314ead636cb4e77adacb4ea0c9824be23b4f4e160dfe62f8c8b22cf","event_uuid":"33aed1d5-72e5-4492-8777-0e2fb5f79eaf","position":{"commit_sha":"7896ec36888fd236c96644437eb75fcf01b8553d","position":"1787946853089295001-33aed1d5-72e5-4492-8777-0e2fb5f79eaf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3929862c2c423c6c918b1dd2df9e09dfaa29264623426cbeedf7db10ac9d4199","event_uuid":"95c2122b-c4c4-4ebb-a823-a053b5fd8374","position":{"commit_sha":"0ee189612a95abc1f8b66ff21cdb3ed7ef625639","position":"1787946863109485001-95c2122b-c4c4-4ebb-a823-a053b5fd8374"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787946853089295001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"95c2122b-c4c4-4ebb-a823-a053b5fd8374","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d284-0454-596a-46c1"}],"description":"## Construct sweep from d284/7dea: shared deterministic .tmp + os.replace across other subsystems\n\nThe shared-deterministic-temp collision class proven in bug 7dea-2f00-db57-4a96 (completion_verdict_cache) and d284-0454-596a-46c1 (plan_review/sizing.save_checkpoint) recurs at other atomic-write sites that derive a temp name deterministically from the target (NOT unique-per-writer via tempfile.mkstemp). Under two concurrent writers for the same target the first os.replace consumes the shared temp and the second raises FileNotFoundError, which each site swallows (log/return) → the losing writer silently loses its own write.\n\n## Candidate sites (semantically confirmed as the same construct; concurrency scenario NOT yet proven live)\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py:191 — `tmp_path = f\"{self.path}.tmp\"` then os.replace; OSError swallowed (warning+return).\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py:375 — identical construct, OSError swallowed.\n- src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py:177 — `tmp = p.with_suffix(p.suffix + \".tmp\")` cursor write; OSError swallowed.\n- Lower-risk (typically single-writer, include only if concurrency is possible):\n  src/rebar/_config_writer.py:279, src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:252 — `target.name + \".tmp\"`.\n  src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py:76 — `f\"{pub_path}.{os.getpid()}.tmp\"` (PID-unique across processes but NOT across threads).\n\nSafe sites already using unique-per-writer mkstemp/mkdtemp (NOT siblings): fsutil.py:77 (the canonical atomic_write seam), completion_verdict_cache.py:229 (7dea fix), sizing.py:770 (d284 fix), snapshot.py, pass_io.py, binding_repository.py, get_rotation.py, staging.py.\n\n## Required work\nFor EACH candidate: (1) determine whether concurrent same-target writers are a real scenario in that subsystem (per-subsystem concurrency analysis — this is why it is not folded into the d284 fix); (2) if yes, apply the proven fix shape (unique same-dir tempfile.mkstemp, atomic replace onto the shared final key, unlink only own temp on failure) or route through the existing src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py atomic_write seam; (3) RED-first regression per site. If concurrency is proven impossible for a site, record that and close it as not-a-bug.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each candidate site has a documented concurrency verdict (live-collision-possible / single-writer-only) with evidence.\n- [ ] Every live-collision site uses a unique-per-writer temp (or the fsutil.atomic_write seam) with a RED-first regression proving two concurrent same-target writers both persist and leave no residue.\n- [ ] Sites proven single-writer are recorded as such (no production change).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["concurrency","cache","atomic-write","sibling-sweep"],"ticket_id":"b3dd-cd97-a052-4ab6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Sibling sweep: shared deterministic .tmp+os.replace collisions in reconciler/review-bot atomic writes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["33aed1d5-72e5-4492-8777-0e2fb5f79eaf","95c2122b-c4c4-4ebb-a823-a053b5fd8374"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787949909435159001,"uuid":"864e0f8c-3ba9-45b2-bdc9-5117b3399ffa"}